# --- jujutsu (colocated repo) ---
# .jj holds jj's own state; never commit it. .git is the colocated backing store.
/.jj/

# --- Nix ---
result
result-*
.direnv/

# --- Go ---
# Binaries / build output (fake providers, executor) live under bin/ or are built ad hoc.
/bin/
*.test
*.out
/coverage.out
# `go build ./cmd/<x>` with no -o drops the binary in the repo root; ignore the
# ones we have (so an ad-hoc build is never accidentally committed).
/nivis
/nivistutor
/provider-alpha
/provider-beta
/provider-delta
/provider-epsilon
/provider-gamma
# Go workspace file is machine-local
go.work
go.work.sum

# --- nivis runtime artifacts ---
# A run writes its state document and, beside it, the outputs ledger. BOTH can
# hold secrets from provider outputs and MUST NOT be committed: the ledger is
# where sensitive outputs live in plaintext by design, because they are kept out
# of the world-readable Nix store. The ledger is 0600; git does not care.
# See docs/IR-CONTRACT.md "Sensitive values across the boundary".
#
# *.ledger is a SUFFIX rule so it follows the file when --state puts it
# elsewhere; the state rule can only cover the default name, which is why nivis
# also reports these paths when a run creates them.
*.ledger
nivis.state.json*

# --- editor / OS noise ---
*.swp
.DS_Store


# goreleaser build output
dist/
/.claude/
